  "code": "2736",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Reactive / Positive:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Indicates past or present infection with Treponema pallidum</li>\n<li>Remains positive even after treatment &mdash; not useful for monitoring treatment response</li>\n<li>Confirms syphilis after a positive non-treponemal test (e.g., RPR, VDRL)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Non-Reactive / Negative:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>No detectable treponemal antibodies</li>\n<li>Rules out syphilis in most cases, unless early window period</li>\n</ul>",
